  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Co-Mining: United in Responsible Copper and Cobalt Mining</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project therefore aims to improve the working conditions, market access and livelihoods, and strengthen the voice of artisanal and small-scale copper and cobalt miners in the Copperbelt and North-Western Provinces (Solwezi District) of Zambia.&#xa0;The project addresses the gender-specific risks and challenges that miners face working in a region with conflict-affected and high-risk area (CAHRA) characteristics, such as informality and illegalization of artisanal and small-scal mining (ASM), gender-based violence and insufficient service provision.</narrative>
  </description>
